    <statement><p>Evaluate the definite integral
<me>\int_{ 0.2 } ^ { 0.4 } 6 \sec^2(x) \, dx</me>
Answer: <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.32049909937694</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>\begin{array}{rcl} \displaystyle \int_{ 0.2 } ^ { 0.4 } 6 \sec^2(x) \, dx 
\amp =\amp  \displaystyle 6  \int_{ 0.2 } ^ { 0.4 }  \sec^2(x) \, dx
\\ \amp =\amp   6  \tan (x) \Big]_{0.2}^{0.4}
\\ \amp =\amp 6 (\tan(0.4)-\tan(0.2)) 
\end{array}</me></p>
</solution>
